<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92403" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιγ-όω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					2.1.17
				</span></i>
			, 
				Ep.
			
			inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ωσέμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.481
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρρίγωσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					3.1
				</span></i>
			.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σ́, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				846
			</span></i>: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρριγωκότες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Ign.</u>
					74
				</span></i>
			 (vv. ll. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρριγότες,
			ἐρριγνωκότες</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				11.556
			</span></i>.—Like <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱδρόω</span>, has
			an irreg. 
				contr.
			 into <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ω</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
				ῳ</span>, for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οι</span>, 3sg.
			subj.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιγῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					517d
				</span></i>
			, cj. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phd.</u>
				85a
			</span></i>; opt. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιγῴη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Int.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.233a
			</span></i>; inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιγῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					1146
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>V.</u>
				446
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Av.</u>
				935
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				440c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				5.1.11
			</span></i>; part. fem. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιγῶσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Semon.
					7.26
				</span></i>
			, but acc. masc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιγοῦντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Vit.</u>
					p.22J.
				</span></i>
			:—<i>to be cold, shiver</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.481
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.92
			</span></i>.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VM</u>
				16
			</span></i>, etc.; though several forms may belong either to this word
			or to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιγέω</span>, as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιγῶν τε καὶ πεινῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					857
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Nu.</u>
				416
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Crates Com.
				33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				517d
			</span></i>.</div>
